  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41301-642975</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41301" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Towards Sustainable Bioeconomy Guidelines (SBG)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall impact of the SBG project is to build FAO&apos;s ability to support both its Member Countries in developing national and regional sustainable bioeconomy strategies, policies and programmes and operators in implementing bioeconomy in a sustainable way. 

The project outcome is the FAO Sustainable Bioeconomy Guidelines to support FAO Member Countries and bioeconomy operators.
The outputs of the project are: 
* Output 1: A report on lessons learned from examples of successful and problematic experiences in bioeconomy development;
* Output 2: A compilation of good bioeconomy practices concerning both the biomass production and the biomass utilization/ biomaterial production stages;
* Output 3: A report on policies to promote good bioeconomy practices; 
* Output 4: A toolbox on sustainable bioeconomy development. 
* Output 5: Agreed indicators to monitor and evaluate the performance  of bioeconomy development; 
* Output 6: Validated FAO sustainable bioeconomy guidelines through regional and specific stakeholder meetings.</narrative>
  </description>
